// Chasm Bridge: Rapier joints as a structure. A rope bridge of 20 timber
// planks, each plank a rigid body hinged to the next and the end planks pinned
// to two sea stacks, sags across a 24 m chasm 13 m above a lava lake. Loads
// drop onto it, each bending the deck further. At once a wood crate with iron
// corners and an iron ingot drops 3.5 m from a stone chute and the deck dips
// into a V and sways. At 3 s a crate of glass bottles drops onto the right
// stack's lip and bursts: its frame splits by Voronoi fracture and the glass
// spills over the end of the deck. From 5 s three charges blast craters in
// the roof and rain rubble on the planks. At 7 s two more cut the ledges under
// an iron-strapped timber block (1.3 t) and it drops flat onto mid-span: the
// deck bows into a deep V and the centre hinge, the only breakable joint
// (17 kN), snaps. Both halves swing down like pendulums against the stack
// faces and hang from their pins. The block plunges into the lava and burns
// down to its iron straps while the crate floats high and chars (wood 60
// against lava 250). At 14 s a last charge blows the right anchor and that
// half drops into the lake and burns. Lit from below by the lava, embers and
// torches, with blue glowshrooms for a cool rim. 10 cells per metre, 60 ticks
// per second: 1260 ticks is 21 s.
[scene]
name = chasm bridge
description = A 20-plank rope bridge of hinged rigid bodies sags over a lava lake. A crate drops on it, a crate of glass bottles bursts at its end, roof charges rain rubble on it and an iron-strapped timber block lands mid-span; the centre hinge snaps, the halves swing down and hang from their pins, the wreckage floats and burns on the lava, and a last charge drops the right half into the lake.
size = 720 380
seed = 0xb21d
ticks = 1260
[build]
fill 0 0 720 380 stone
// one big cavern: ragged roof, open down to the lava lake
terrain 0 720 50 10 37 air 284
circle 60 46 28 air
circle 165 38 24 air
circle 560 42 26 air
circle 665 48 28 air
